From 72b1c1053d1075df654a9e3c60e3081ab39e1dc9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cameron Sparks <cam@sparksd.net>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 08:55:52 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] mime: validate subparts before freeing the part's content

Curl_mime_set_subparts freed the part's existing content before it
checked the new subparts. If the subparts handle was nested inside the
tree the part already owned, it was freed first and then dereferenced by
the checks.

Run the attached, root and rewind checks first and return their error
without touching the part. Clean up the old content only once they pass,
or directly when subparts is NULL.

Extend lib643 with a case that sets a part's subparts to a mime nested
inside them, and checks that the call fails and leaves the part's
subparts in place.

Closes #24047

Upstream: https://github.com/curl/curl/commit/72b1c1053d1075df654a9e3c60e3081ab39e1dc9
---
 lib/mime.c | 8 +++++---
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/lib/mime.c b/lib/mime.c
index f491f22..fb6055b 100644
--- a/lib/mime.c
+++ b/lib/mime.c
@@ -1511,9 +1511,9 @@ CURLcode Curl_mime_set_subparts(curl_mimepart *part,
   if(part->kind == MIMEKIND_MULTIPART && part->arg == subparts)
     return CURLE_OK;
 
-  cleanup_part_content(part);
-
-  if(subparts) {
+  if(!subparts)
+    cleanup_part_content(part);
+  else {
     /* Should not have been attached already. */
     if(subparts->parent)
       return CURLE_BAD_FUNCTION_ARGUMENT;
@@ -1537,6 +1537,8 @@ CURLcode Curl_mime_set_subparts(curl_mimepart *part,
        CURL_SEEKFUNC_OK)
       return CURLE_SEND_FAIL_REWIND;
 
+    cleanup_part_content(part);
+
     subparts->parent = part;
     /* Subparts are processed internally: no read callback. */
     part->seekfunc = mime_subparts_seek;
